+;; Test MemProf context disambiguation when tail calls target GlobalAliases
+;; (both imported via replaceAliasWithAliasee, where the imported function
+;; intentionally retains the aliasee's !guid metadata, and within the defining
+;; module itself).
+;;
+;; Covered scenarios:
+;; 1. a.ll (a.o): Direct tail call to imported external alias (@alias_func)
+;;    WITHOUT @aliasee imported.
+;; 2. e.ll (e.o) & c.ll (c.o): Direct tail call to imported external alias
+;;    (@alias_func) when @aliasee IS also imported into the module:
+;;    - e.o: @aliasee imported as a DECLARATION (via
+;;      -memprof-import-cloned-indirect-targets).
+;;    - c.o: @aliasee imported as an available_externally DEFINITION.
+;; 3. d.ll (d.o): Direct tail call to imported promoted internal alias
+;;    (@local_alias.llvm.* imported along with caller @b_helper).
+;; 4. b.ll (b.o): Same-module direct tail call (@b_same_mod_mid) to a
+;;    GlobalAlias (@alias_func) in the defining module.
